# RPost workflow

- The only content stages are topic and post.
- `topics/index.json` is the topic data source; `topics/index.md` is its generated reading view. Posts live in numbered folders under `content/posts/`.
- Read shared prompts through `prompt-rules/index.json`.
- Automatically choose one fixed category slug: `r-plot`, `r-stats`, `r-base`, `r-tidyverse`, or `r-code-management`.
- Generate a post directly from a selected topic number or free-form subject.
- Preserve explicit user-provided headings, order, examples, and output requirements; they override prompt defaults.
- Update JSON article metadata and regenerate the Markdown view when a candidate becomes an article.
- Never create a permanent images folder; rendered Markdown embeds images.
- Do not add scheduling, queue, rank, or automatic daily writing fields.
- Follow the full repository contract in `AGENTS.md`.
